{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 27, :comments ["<b>And I am dust and ashes.</b> By way of the plain sense (peshat): <b>and I am dust</b> I was, <b>and ashes</b> I shall again be, and this is the confession of the righteous. And so David, peace be upon him, said (Psalms 103): ״כי הוא ידע יצרנו״ — ״זכור כי עפר אנחנו״. And so Job said (Job 42): ״על כן אמאס ונחמתי על עפר ואפר״." "<b>And by way of</b> the Midrash: in the merit that Abraham said ״ואנכי עפר ואפר״, his descendants merited two commandments: the dust of the sotah and the ashes of the red heifer. And likewise we find that all Israel are called by the name Ephraim, as it is said (Jeremiah 31): ״הבן יקיר לי אפרים״ — this is as if it said אפרים as two אפרים: the ashes of Abraham and the ashes of Isaac."], :book :genesis, :voice :rabbeinu-bahya, :lang :en, :chapter 18, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-30T14:13:26.960303305Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}